Z||000002||Tigger||11-26-2001||09:38 PM||||Never know, it could be one of those Fiero Gremlins!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000003||TRiAD||11-26-2001||09:42 PM||||I've heard they dislike mothballs, but you may not appreciate the smell either...<P>Sorry.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tina||11-26-2001||09:45 PM||||Mouse trap?<P>Really don't know,sorry.<BR>But as a fellow Mouse damage victim,<BR>(never found the mouse,just the nest in the rear bumper and a 2 inch hole in the heating system)<BR>all I can say is get it out of there <B>fast</B><P>Tina||||reg||1
Z||000005||Mach10||11-26-2001||09:51 PM||||Hate the buggers.<P>Although I hate saying it, lay down poison. That's the fastest way to stop the PERMANENT damage... Unfortunately, they tend to find somewhere inconvenient to die... So there's a chance that it may smell a little funky come spring. <P>The other alternative is to stuff steel wool into the vents and any access places. ESPECIALLY at the front firewall. Heater core gives a nice way in. Stuff with steel wool. Ditto for vents, and drains. After you're done this, lay down 3-4 snap-traps  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/~treme_sports.jpg">  <BR>||||reg||10
Z||000006||hugh||11-26-2001||10:16 PM||||Open the hood,throw in a cat,close the hood real fast.||||reg||12
Z||000007||DRH||11-26-2001||11:27 PM||||Poison and/or trap ASAP! If there's not already more than one there soon will be. A parked car is an attractive apartment building to mice this time of year. Peanut butter works pretty good on the simple mouse traps.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Adrift||11-26-2001||11:52 PM||||How does a mouse get into a car? ||||reg||1
Z||000009||Standard||11-26-2001||11:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by hugh:<BR><B>Open the hood,throw in a cat,close the hood real fast.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>aaaaahahahahaha!  I almost fell out of my chair when I read that!<P><BR>I've heard they don't like the laundry freshener sheet thingies for some reason.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000010||sailordude||11-27-2001||12:12 AM||||When I first bought my car this past spring I was driving it home and it started to lose power.  Anyway after the $150 tow home it cost me another $400 to get a new cat converter in my car because my old one was full of fried up mouse bodies and their nest.  Quite a bummer.  Moral of the story...get rid of them quick!!!<P>Best of luck to you man||||reg||1
Z||000011||TylerB11||11-27-2001||12:13 AM||||Why are you complaining? you have an engineer living onboard to keep an eye on that 2.8! Seriously, starting the car usually scares the Sh*t out of them, and out of the car.||||reg||1
Z||000012||watts||11-27-2001||12:49 AM||||TOO FUNNY!!!!!<P>When I first bought my car, it had been sitting parked for about 6 years untouched, except for the guy who broke the drivers side glass a few years before.  I fixed up a bunch of basic things on it and started driving it.  <P>A day or so after I started using it, I noticed more little black things on the floor - I thought it was more dirt falling from under the dash or something.  Then I noticed the little pile of grey plastic dust behind the seats by the rear plastic panels!   Arghhhh!!!  MICE!<P>Parked it inside my garage that night.  One 'live mouse trap' sitting on a bit of wood on the floor with some ham in it.  Found mister mouse in the trap the next morning...  dead...  seems he was so BIG (I guess Fiero parts are nourishing!) that since he of course went in head first, he filled up the whole trap and suffocated.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>So much for a live trap.<BR><P>------------------<BR>87/88 V6 5spd Notchback Hybrid<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/watts_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||Ali_Gulf_Fiero||11-27-2001||08:24 AM||||Why would you want to get rid of him?<BR>Now you get to boast to your friends of your Fiero with 140 horsepower and 1 mousepower!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>my cat's sitting in my scrambled eggs.||||reg||10
Z||000014||Oreif||11-27-2001||08:50 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by hugh:<BR><B>Open the hood,throw in a cat,close the hood real fast.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah, But once the cat eats the mouse, how does he get rid of the cat? Throw in a dog?<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>(Isn't there a children's song that goes something like that?)<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 11-27-2001).]||||reg||1
