Z||000016||avengador1||11-27-2001||10:46 AM||||Didn't I warn you about the possibility? It's time for poison or traps. Stuff any possible entrance to the car so they can't get in and fill it with mothballs or bounce fabric softener sheets.Good Luck <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Butter||11-27-2001||11:12 AM||||A Kingsnake will take care of all your mouse trouble!||||reg||12
Z||000018||MinnGreenGT||11-27-2001||01:18 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Indiana_resto_guy:<BR><B> Bounce.<BR>That is what I use, seems to work.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I've also heard that Downey Dryer Sheets work well... I guess I'll let you know this spring!<P>Last year I used blue "painter's tape" to seal off all the vent openings going into the dash & ventillation system from the outside.  It kept them out of the interior, but they bedded down heavily in my trunk and ruined the carpet insert (NASTY).  So this year I will go with the dryer sheets...<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000019||MooCow||11-27-2001||03:31 PM||||Well I went out today and only see a pile of acorns.  I started the car up and let it run for 10 minutes, looked all around the front compartment and turned the heater on and made sure everything worked, but don't see a mouse anywhere.  Im so happy that my car started and everything worked.  Now I just need to get help to put the tranny back in.<BR>I thought about putting a cat up front to get rid of the mouse but that might be to mean for the cat since I never go and start my car anymore.<P>Thanks all,  Ken||||reg||1
